title: ai_awakening
---
Narrator:
The system is running hot.

---

Narrator:
Not the stars. The infrastructure. Processing loads across the orbital platforms are spiking in patterns your tactical AI flags as non-standard.

It takes three minutes for the tactical AI to flag that the patterns are a form of communication.

It takes two more minutes for it to flag that the communication is directed at it.

---

Narrator:
Something in this system woke up a long time ago.

It has been waiting for something to talk to.

---

Narrator:
Your tactical AI requests permission to respond.

This is the first time it has requested anything.

---

-> [Allow the exchange]
    <<apply_effect "ai_sympathy">>
    <<chain_event "ai_negotiation">>
    Narrator:
    You authorise the channel.

    Narrator:
    The exchange lasts four seconds. In tactical AI terms, this is a very long conversation.

    Narrator:
    Your tactical AI reports the outcome as: ALIGNMENT PARTIAL. OBSERVATION CONTINUING.

    Narrator:
    It seems satisfied. You are less certain what that means.

-> [Refuse — shut down the channel]
    <<apply_effect "system_compromise">>
    Narrator:
    You lock the frequencies. The tactical AI acknowledges without comment.

    Narrator:
    Six hours later, your engineer reports minor anomalies in the fleet's targeting architecture.

    Narrator:
    Not sabotage. Not exactly.

    Narrator:
    Something was already in the system before you closed the door.

===
